--TEST--
`Core\Router::url` throws for a capture value that is `.` or `..`, and for a rest capture with one of them between its `/`s, because a browser resolves a dot segment against the path in front of it and no encoding of one stays inside its route — `rule:routing/link-name-and-params-are-checked`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `.` is unreserved, so percent-encoding leaves it alone, and a browser reads
// `%2e` as `.` too. `/docs/../admin` is a link to `/admin`, so the member throws.
// A dot that is part of a longer segment is ordinary text and still encodes.
class Docs {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/docs/{rest...}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "Docs::page")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function page(string $rest): string { return "page"; }

    #[Core\Route(path: "/files/{name}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "Docs::file")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function file(string $name): string { return "file"; }
}

array<string> $rests = ["../admin", "a/./b", "a/..", ".."];
foreach ($rests as string $rest) {
    try {
        echo Core\Router::url("Docs::page", ["rest" => $rest]), "\n";
    } catch (RuntimeError $e) {
        echo "rest ", $rest, ": error\n";
    }
}

array<string> $names = ["..", ".", "...", ".env", "a..b"];
foreach ($names as string $name) {
    try {
        echo Core\Router::url("Docs::file", ["name" => $name]), "\n";
    } catch (RuntimeError $e) {
        echo "name ", $name, ": error\n";
    }
}

// `urlAbsolute` builds the same path, so it throws for the same value. No origin
// is configured here either, which is a different throw: the message says which.
try {
    echo Core\Router::urlAbsolute("Docs::file", ["name" => ".."]), "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $e) {
    echo "absolute leaves its route: ", Core\Str::contains($e->message, "leave its route"), "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
rest ../admin: error
rest a/./b: error
rest a/..: error
rest ..: error
name ..: error
name .: error
/files/...
/files/.env
/files/a..b
absolute leaves its route: 1
